<div class="tab-content"><br>
<div id="detailsTabContent" class="tab-pane active">

    <dl id="descriptorDetails_NonlinearDynamics"
        class="dl-horizontal">

        <dt>MeSH Heading      </dt>

        <dd>Nonlinear Dynamics</dd>

        
                    <dt>Tree Number(s)</dt>
                    
                        <dd><a id="treeNumber_0" onclick=
                               "switchTab([ 'trees', 'treesTabContent' ])"
                            >E05.599.850</a></dd>
                    
                        <dd><a id="treeNumber_1" onclick=
                               "switchTab([ 'trees', 'treesTabContent' ])"
                            >H01.548.675</a></dd>
                    

        <dt>Unique ID</dt><dd>D017711</dd>

        <dt>RDF Unique Identifier</dt>
        <dd><a href="https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D017711.html">
            http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D017711
        </a></dd>

        <span id="annotation">
            <dt>Annotation</dt><dd>a math principle applied to theoret models</dd>
        </span>
                <span id="scopeNote">
                    <dt>Scope Note</dt><dd>The study of systems which respond disproportionately (nonlinearly) to initial conditions or perturbing stimuli. Nonlinear systems may exhibit chaos which is classically characterized as sensitive dependence on initial conditions. Chaotic systems, while distinguished from more ordered periodic systems, are not random. When their behavior over time is appropriately displayed (in phase space), constraints are evident which are described by strange attractors. Phase space representations of chaotic systems, or strange attractors, usually reveal fractal (<a href="/record/ui?ui=D017709" class="textLink_FRACTALS">FRACTALS</a>) self-similarity across time scales. Natural, including biological, systems often display nonlinear dynamics and chaos.</dd>
                </span>
            
                <dt>Entry Term(s)</dt>
                <dd>
                    Chaos Theory
                    
                </dd><dd>
                    Models, Nonlinear
                    
                </dd><dd>
                    Non-linear Dynamics
                    
                </dd><dd>
                    Non-linear Models
                    
                </dd>
                <dt>Previous Indexing</dt>
                
                    <dd>Mathematics (1974-1993)</dd>
                
                    <dd>Models, Biological (1970-1993)</dd>
                
                <dt>See Also</dt>
                
                    <dd><a id="seeAlso_Fractals"
                           href="/record/ui?ui=D017709"
                        >Fractals</a></dd>
                
            <dt>Public MeSH Note</dt><dd>94</dd>
        
            <dt>History Note</dt><dd>94</dd>
        
        


        
                <dt>Date Introduced</dt>
                <dd>1994/01/01</dd>
            
                <dt>Last Updated</dt>
                <dd>2008/07/08</dd>
            

    </dl>

</div>

